\citation{yang2018hotpotqa}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Main comparison on BEIR SciFact (148 documents through the production pipeline; 30 official queries and qrels). Rows 1--2 are the suite channels (Module B); rows 3--10 are the reproduced DeepRead-style systems, answered through one shared agent under a uniform 4{,}000-character evidence budget and graded 0--10 by an independent agent given the gold document (Judge). The right two columns come from an HTTP-driven rerun that is byte-identical to the offline run (480/480 checks); a middle agent ranks the eight anonymised answers per question, 1 = best of 8. Setting reproduced from \citet  {li2026deepread}.}}{8}{table.caption.23}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:deepread}{{2}{8}{Main comparison on BEIR SciFact (148 documents through the production pipeline; 30 official queries and qrels). Rows 1--2 are the suite channels (Module B); rows 3--10 are the reproduced DeepRead-style systems, answered through one shared agent under a uniform 4{,}000-character evidence budget and graded 0--10 by an independent agent given the gold document (Judge). The right two columns come from an HTTP-driven rerun that is byte-identical to the offline run (480/480 checks); a middle agent ranks the eight anonymised answers per question, 1 = best of 8. Setting reproduced from \citet {li2026deepread}}{table.caption.23}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Component ablation on BEIR SciFact (30 queries, official qrels), same query set as Table\nonbreakingspace \ref {tab:deepread}. ``Deep'' variants re-rank a $k{=}40$ pool, because the deployed top-10 is already pre-filtered by the Stage-3 threshold (lowest returned score $0.379$), making a shallow-pool threshold sweep a no-op --- itself a finding. Rows omitted for space ($k{=}5$, no-dedup, and the two other deep threshold values) are in the released artefact.}}{8}{table.caption.27}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:ablation}{{3}{8}{Component ablation on BEIR SciFact (30 queries, official qrels), same query set as Table~\ref {tab:deepread}. ``Deep'' variants re-rank a $k{=}40$ pool, because the deployed top-10 is already pre-filtered by the Stage-3 threshold (lowest returned score $0.379$), making a shallow-pool threshold sweep a no-op --- itself a finding. Rows omitted for space ($k{=}5$, no-dedup, and the two other deep threshold values) are in the released artefact}{table.caption.27}{}}
